[2026-10-25T10:23:04.565Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"reasoning","text":"**Designing geometry options**\n\nI need to work on a thoughtful geometry design that defaults like previous examples but is close to the gallery. I'm thinking about the screenshots to ensure they feature free symmetric straight diagonals with specific parameters. \n\nIt seems logical to introduce a new geometry editor flag to address past export needs while keeping the URLs unchanged. I also want to make sure users can easily navigate the editor with options for legacy modes and new bend semantics without confusion. Keeping user experience in mind is so important!\n**Adjusting geometry parameters**\n\nI’m setting up balanced default parameters with specific angles, tension, bulge, and gaps. The starting offset of 2.5 needs to create a true cross shape, extending the bar correctly. \n\nI think I could replace the bar and line with a more stable cross marker that features two perpendicular strokes. It's essential to ensure it maintains symmetry based on the configuration. The user should have the option to choose \"cross\" as a start shape, while retaining the bar structure for clarity.\n**Aligning screenshot defaults**\n\nI need to make sure that users have a default selection of a bar for screenshots since the default cross option isn't matching the dropdown. \n\nURLs should align with the settings users expect, and the default should clearly be set to the bar with an offset of 2.5. I can add a cross as an optional feature, but it might not be necessary. I also want to make sure that geometric tests are strict so everything aligns as intended, keeping symmetry and accuracy at the forefront."}}
