ption":"Improvements or additions to documentation","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":8113453904,"node_id":"LA_kwDON1sLX88AAAAB45l7UA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","color":"a2eeef","default":true,"description":"New feature or request","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-10-25T10:17:32Z","updated_at":"2026-10-25T10:19:08Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"See these screenshots carefully:\n<img width=\"1824\" height=\"1112\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/769b3d28-36ff-4d4b-abe2-4faa97d0e756\" />\n\nhttps://konard.github.io/network/?code=1122&sourceAngle=24&targetAngle=40&tension=0.4&bulge=25&startGap=0.09&startOffset=2.9\n\n<img width=\"1824\" height=\"1112\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/10a189a9-0ff5-4bf6-9227-7a0aa09b2cfc\" />\n\nhttps://konard.github.io/network/?code=00000000&bulge=19&padding=10&startOffset=2.5\n\nWe also need to double check that all settings on screenshots perfectly match resulting links and vice versa.\n\nI want when clicked on links networks configurations across the website, we have default geometry closer to these examples. For some reason our bend setting is not universal, and is more of rotation than bend. Meaning it is not possible to have single setting at the moment, that looks perfectly all the time, and I want to by default in all configurations that it looks perfectly and close to how we show in list of all links networks configurations.\n\nStart of the link should now have cross-like shape as per configuration. We should have strict tests that the shape looks perfectly symmetrical when possible.\n\nAnd also colors must be the same as in the links network configuration clicked at other places of the website. Also we should not do underscore on hover when we browser links network configuration. So no surprises for the user. It should get as close visual to what he clicked as possible.\n\nIn this pull request please focus on updating geometry only affecting the editor of single network after sharing, as it is critical not to break all other geometry drawings, across the website.\n\nWe need to download all logs and data related about the issue to this repository, make sure we compile that data to `./docs/case-studies/issue-{id}` folder, and use it to do deep case study analysis (also make sure to search online for additional facts and data), in which we will reconstruct timeline/sequence of events, list of each and all requirements from the issue, find root causes of the each problem, and propose possible solutions and solution plans for each requirement (we should also check known existing components/libraries, that solve similar problem or can help in solutions).\n\nIf there is not enough data to find actual root cause, add debug output and verbose mode if not present, that will allow us to find root cause on next iteration.\n\nIf issue related to any other repository/project, where we can report issues on GitHub, please do so. Each issue must contain reproducible examples, workarounds and suggestions for fix the issue in code. Also double check to fully apply requirements to entire codebase, so if we have issue in multiple places, it should be fixed in all them.\n\nPlease plan and execute everything in this single pull request, you have unlimited time and context, as context auto-compacts and you can continue indefinitely, until it is each and every requirement fully addressed, and everything is totally done.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/issues/21/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/issues/21/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}[[]]{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/pulls/22","id":5003861836,"node_id":"PR_kwDON1sLX88AAAABKkDfTA","html_url":"https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/pull/22","diff_url":"https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/pull/22.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/pull/22.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/issues/22","number":22,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Make editor geometry symmetric and preserve source colors","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixes #21.\n\nClicking a network now opens the editor with symmetric loop defaults, cross-like starts and the colors shown at the source. Bend changes free-link curvature and self-loop width; free endpoints stay anchored. Gallery, theory and background-rain geometry retain their original construction.\n\n- Match dark/light colors from gallery cards, share icons and theory examples; remove gallery hover underlines.\n- Preserve independent angles, gaps, marker controls, placements, overlap reduction, exports and saved styles. Keep legacy tangent rotation selectable and recognize older explicit custom-color URLs.\n- Verify both supplied URLs against their controls, then edit/share/reload to the same SVG. The screenshot values already parsed correctly; inherited defaults and bend construction caused the differences.\n\n### Reproduction and verification\n\nOpen `/network/?code=1122` and `/network/?code=00000000`, vary Bend, and compare with gallery navigation. Equal endpoint angles/gaps give point-symmetric loops; free endpoints no longer rotate with Bend. Also hover a gallery card and open it in both themes.\n\nAutomated coverage: `src/links/geometry-21.test.js`, `src/pages/network-21.test.jsx`, and `npm run test:network:issue21`. Strict symmetry samples, all 4,181 small editor configurations, and 4,693 unchanged gallery/rain SVG hashes guard geometry and scope. Browser checks verify supplied settings, share/reload, dark/light navigation, hover, SVG export and mobile overflow.\n\nValidation: 693 unit tests pass; repository checks and production build pass; Chromium, Firefox and WebKit pass the new and existing browser suites. CI also verifies CV PDFs and the Pages build artifact.\n\n### Before / after\n\n| Original editor | Updated editor |\n| --- | --- |\n| ![Before: unequal loops and different colors](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-21-823573f25e74/docs/case-studies/issue-21/screenshots/chromium-before-default-1122.png?raw=true) | ![After: symmetric loops and matching colors](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-21-823573f25e74/docs/case-studies/issue-21/screenshots/chromium-after-default-1122.png?raw=true) |\n| ![Before: rotated free links](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-21-823573f25e74/docs/case-studies/issue-21/screenshots/chromium-before-default-00000000.png?raw=true) | ![After: anchored curves and cross starts](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-21-823573f25e74/docs/case-studies/issue-21/screenshots/chromium-after-default-00000000.png?raw=true) |\n\n![Editor controls with the first supplied configuration](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-21-823573f25e74/docs/case-studies/issue-21/screenshots/chromium-after-supplied-1.png?raw=true)\n\n[Complete case study, settings audit, requirement inventory, timeline, root causes, library research, raw logs/data and browser evidence](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/tree/issue-21-823573f25e74/docs/case-studies/issue-21). All causes were traced to this application; no external dependency defect required an upstream report.\n","created_at":"2026-10-25T10:21:12Z","updated_at":"2026-10-25T10:44:52Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"ad14e5ae0de11bfd9486d86f324213845bcd6c2b","assignees":[{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":fa